WEBVTT

NOTE Draft timings; synchronize with recorded voice before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
A question begins at home.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Why has the water around us changed?

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Curiosity is a beginning.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Understanding needs opportunities to learn, and people who listen.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Digital tools connect more of our world.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
But access to technology is not the same as capability.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
We must understand its limits, and remain responsible for our decisions.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Families, teachers and universities help us ask better questions, compare evidence and develop judgement.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Learning becomes useful when we can explain not only an answer, but why we trust it.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Practice connects knowledge with real needs.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Teams may explore monitoring, data and infrastructure.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Their work must be tested, documented and connected to appropriate professional expertise.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.000
A useful solution needs more than technology.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Institutions must agree who operates it, maintains it and reviews the information.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.000
Governance connects authority with safeguards and accountability.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Communities must be heard.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:07.000
Independent capability grows when local people can adapt, maintain and teach what they use.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Experience returns to education and public decisions, revealing what works and what still needs to change.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:19.000
Smart World Education connects these steps: education, understanding, practical application and independent capability.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Explore how one person's learning becomes part of a whole society's development.
